[{:db/id "q-255829/field-1/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" :answer/id #uuid "fb358225-fed0-5e9b-b4af-20d816c3089e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186090169 :answer-field/correct "q-255829/field-1/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" :answer-field/choices ["q-255829/field-1/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-255829"] :question/problem "Given that the function $f(x)={e}^{x}-4{x}^{2}$ has a root in the interval $[0,1],$ use the Netwon-Raphson process starting from ${x}_{0}=1$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to one decimal place.\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({e}^{x}-4{x}^{2})^{′}={e}^{x}-8x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-4{x}_{n}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-8{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}({e}^{{x}_{n}}-8{x}_{n})-({e}^{{x}_{n}}-4{x}_{n}^{2})}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-8{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}{e}^{{x}_{n}}-{e}^{{x}_{n}}-4{x}_{n}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-8{x}_{n}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{{x}_{0}{e}^{{x}_{0}}-{e}^{{x}_{0}}-4{x}_{0}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{0}}-8{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1{e}^{1}-{e}^{1}-4(1)^{2}}{{e}^{1}-8(1)} \\\\  & =0.757….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}}-{e}^{{x}_{1}}-4{x}_{1}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{1}}-8{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.757…){e}^{0.757…}-{e}^{0.757…}-4(0.757…)^{2}}{{e}^{0.757…}-8(0.757…)} \\\\  & =0.716…, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{2}}-{e}^{{x}_{2}}-4{x}_{2}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{2}}-8{x}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.716…){e}^{0.716…}-{e}^{0.716…}-4(0.716…)^{2}}{{e}^{0.716…}-8(0.716…)} \\\\  & =0.714….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{2}≈0.7$ and ${x}_{3}≈0.7$ are the same when rounded to one decimal place.\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x≈0.7,$ rounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-256499/field-1/05389455732ee97e4034837e7bc6793766e3474da9cbfe3d3bc189061b9816ab" :answer/id #uuid "d7d43193-41ba-5561-b72f-1169b59eeecf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.941" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-256499/field-1/f23eceaa3b669660e4c1e985b937b149459e9fb8b9b1169b5178c20408e2da0b" :answer/id #uuid "101819d9-9c53-5b72-bdc0-f1a3d288331a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.086" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-256499/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "72c4cdea-d5a5-5a81-90dc-580413713ffc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-256499/field-1/05389455732ee97e4034837e7bc6793766e3474da9cbfe3d3bc189061b9816ab" :answer-field/choices ["q-256499/field-1/05389455732ee97e4034837e7bc6793766e3474da9cbfe3d3bc189061b9816ab" "q-256499/field-1/f23eceaa3b669660e4c1e985b937b149459e9fb8b9b1169b5178c20408e2da0b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-256499" :question/id #uuid "463b09ce-6793-58e9-8703-1735cc39c980" :question/math-academy-id "q-256499" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-10{x}^{2}+8$ in the interval $[0,1].$ Calculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point ${x}_{0}=0.5.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n${x}_{2}≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({x}^{4}-10{x}^{2}+8)^{′}=4{x}^{3}-20x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}_{n}^{4}-10{x}_{n}^{2}+8}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-20{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(4{x}_{n}^{3}-20{x}_{n})-({x}_{n}^{4}-10{x}_{n}^{2}+8)}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-20{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}_{n}^{4}-10{x}_{n}^{2}-8}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-20{x}_{n}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=0.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{3{x}_{0}^{4}-10{x}_{0}^{2}-8}{4{x}_{0}^{3}-20{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(0.5)^{4}-10(0.5)^{2}-8}{4(0.5)^{3}-20(0.5)} \\\\  & =1.085\\,526…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{3{x}_{n}^{4}-10{x}_{n}^{2}-8}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-20{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1.085\\,526…)^{4}-10(1.085\\,526…)^{2}-8}{4(1.085\\,526…)^{3}-20(1.085\\,526…)} \\\\  & ≈0.941,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-256499/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f482b25-8a5b-5aed-93bb-68c2bcdcb713"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-256499"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-256529/field-1/8621d82a3537f3b1a47ef5037d95365704e527898dfc58a877ed417de48c422b" :answer/id #uuid "59d136a5-e319-55bd-83b7-22d0e2ea32e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.259" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-256529/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "62a05b2f-7d8c-527b-9492-8a470ab8f29f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-256529/field-1/8621d82a3537f3b1a47ef5037d95365704e527898dfc58a877ed417de48c422b" :answer-field/choices ["q-256529/field-1/8621d82a3537f3b1a47ef5037d95365704e527898dfc58a877ed417de48c422b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-256529" :question/id #uuid "3fb88b0e-02a0-54d6-bc94-435c03f1aa79" :question/math-academy-id "q-256529" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x$ in the interval $[1,2].$ Calculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point ${x}_{0}=1.23.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n${x}_{2}≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x)^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{n}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{n}-{x}_{n}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{n}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{n}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1.23,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{0}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{0}-{x}_{0}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{0}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{0}-1} \\\\  & =1.23-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1.23)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.23)-1.23}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.23)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1.23)-1} \\\\  & =1.259\\,054…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{1}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{1}-{x}_{1}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{1}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{1}-1} \\\\  & =1.259\\,054…-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1.259\\,054…)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.259\\,054…)-1.259\\,054…}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.259\\,054…)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1.259\\,054…)-1} \\\\  & ≈1.259,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-256529/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f482b25-8a5b-5aed-93bb-68c2bcdcb713"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-256529"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-256604/field-1/b84fd199de02d074681f284eb5fe7f2e716d60e640d03dab08be8c2ffb95c521" :answer/id #uuid "8348c36a-2df6-5f5a-857a-8aeb7125a2ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-256604/field-1/1953fffdd5464c00598a8fc81fdbe9a25a6903f89c460eaf7b2d56ffaf15695e" :answer/id #uuid "5cdf0bd9-97b5-560f-b074-39fce1818745" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-256604/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1120b53b-eefa-551b-9636-cef5a9c7dbce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-256604/field-1/b84fd199de02d074681f284eb5fe7f2e716d60e640d03dab08be8c2ffb95c521" :answer-field/choices ["q-256604/field-1/b84fd199de02d074681f284eb5fe7f2e716d60e640d03dab08be8c2ffb95c521" "q-256604/field-1/1953fffdd5464c00598a8fc81fdbe9a25a6903f89c460eaf7b2d56ffaf15695e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-256604" :question/id #uuid "1bb57f93-6f6f-525e-968e-2594a6438da3" :question/math-academy-id "q-256604" :question/problem "Given that the function $f(x)={x}^{3}-x-4$ has a root in the interval $[1,2],$ use the Newton-Raphson process starting from ${x}_{0}=1.5$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to one decimal place.\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({x}^{3}-x-4)^{′}=3{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}_{n}^{3}-x-4}{3{x}_{n}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(3{x}_{n}^{2}-1)-({x}_{n}^{3}-{x}_{n}-4)}{3{x}_{n}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}_{n}^{3}+4}{3{x}_{n}^{2}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{2{x}_{0}^{3}+4}{3{x}_{0}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.5)^{3}+4}{3(1.5)^{2}-1} \\\\  & =1.869…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{2{x}_{1}^{3}+4}{3{x}_{1}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.869…)^{3}+4}{3(1.869…)^{2}-1} \\\\  & =1.799…, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{2{x}_{2}^{3}+4}{3{x}_{2}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.799…)^{3}+4}{3(1.799…)^{2}-1} \\\\  & =1.796….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{2}≈1.8$ and ${x}_{3}≈1.8$ are the same when rounded to one decimal place.\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x≈1.8,$ rounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-256604/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f5b59d4-11de-519e-99fb-5490018d5225"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-256604"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-256616/field-1/cee0db0ce503f760b910d870ecb7ba6235a13f11a3aa39305618810075a7ef48" :answer/id #uuid "6095af9e-464b-59e3-a318-456167606b42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.619" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186090173 :answer-field/correct "q-256616/field-1/cee0db0ce503f760b910d870ecb7ba6235a13f11a3aa39305618810075a7ef48" :answer-field/choices ["q-256616/field-1/cee0db0ce503f760b910d870ecb7ba6235a13f11a3aa39305618810075a7ef48"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-256616"] :question/problem "Given that the function $f(x)={e}^{x}-3x$ has a root in the interval $[0,1],$ use the Newton-Raphson process starting from ${x}_{0}=0.2$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to three decimal places.\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({e}^{x}-3x)^{′}={e}^{x}-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-3{x}_{n}}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}({e}^{{x}_{n}}-3)-({e}^{{x}_{n}}-3{x}_{n})}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n}-1)}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=0.2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{0}}({x}_{0}-1)}{{e}^{{x}_{0}}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0.2}(0.2-1)}{{e}^{0.2}-3} \\\\  & =0.5493….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}-1)}{{e}^{{x}_{1}}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0.5493…}(0.5493…-1)}{{e}^{0.5493…}-3} \\\\  & =0.6156…, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}-1)}{{e}^{{x}_{2}}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0.6156…}(0.6156…-1)}{{e}^{0.6156…}-3} \\\\  & =0.6190…, \\\\ {x}_{4} & =\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{3}}({x}_{3}-1)}{{e}^{{x}_{3}}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0.6190…}(0.6190…-1)}{{e}^{0.6190…}-3} \\\\  & =0.6190….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{3}≈0.619$ and ${x}_{4}≈0.619$ are the same when rounded to three decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x≈0.619,$ rounded to three decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
